  "method": "Denominator = top-level frontier sessions from the agents' own transcripts, independent of HEARTH. Claude: ~/.claude/projects/<projdir>/<uuid>.jsonl, UUID-named files only, nothing under a subagents/ directory; day = UTC date of the first line carrying a timestamp (mtime if none); session id = the sessionId field (file stem if absent); prompts = user lines that are not tool_result echoes and not isMeta/isSidechain. Codex: ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl, day = directory path, prompts = role=user response_item messages excluding injected context (AGENTS.md, environment, instructions); null when the rollout shows no message items. Eligible = >= 3 prompts and cc-<first 8 of sessionId> not in knowledge/rd-task-ids.json. used_hearth (Claude only): the session's cc- id is a key of knowledge/offload.json by_task or a string task_id in the execution events.ndjson (read-only). in_lane (Claude only): an amux sessions/*.meta.json cc_conversation_id[:8] equals sessionId[:8]. Both are shares of claude_eligible and are not independent: do not multiply them. Codex sessions are not joined (no cc- id; the cx-<lane> stamp starts with I1.2). Windows are UTC days, last 14 including today.",
  "caveats": [
    "offload.json by_task is truncated (25 task ids omitted); the events.ndjson join covers the gap, but used_hearth can still undercount."
